{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — NEWSLETTER CONFIRMATION (2026-09-04)
  Assign this template to the page with handle `newsletter-confirmation`.

  ═══ WHY IT EXISTS ═══
  The homepage newsletter form used to fake success with a JS toast and discard
  the email. It is now a real {% form 'customer' %} that redirects here on
  form.posted_successfully?, so this page is the ONLY confirmation a subscriber
  ever sees. It has to actually confirm something, set expectations, and give a
  warm visitor somewhere to go — a bare "thanks" wastes the highest-intent
  moment this person will have.

  ═══ TRAPS THIS FILE AVOIDS (same three as page.start-here.liquid) ═══
  1. COLOURS ARE INVERTED site-wide by snippets/lbass-stamp.liquid — `--cream`
     resolves to #0B0B0C. Writing against token names here renders light-on-light.
     Every colour below is a literal hex: dark text on the bone page (#F2F0EB).
  2. lbass-stamp sets a global `h1 { ... !important }`. A plain `.nc-hero h1`
     loses that cascade, so the H1 is styled at (0,2,1) + !important.
  3. templates/page.pseo.liquid does NOT render {{ page.content }}. This one DOES,
     so the copy stays editable in Admin without a developer.

  ═══ INDEXING ═══
  layout/theme.liquid forces noindex,follow for this handle. A confirmation page
  is thin, reachable only after a POST, and must never compete in search.
{%- endcomment -%}

